{
  "_readme": "Maps each CM5 native-MQTT-Publisher topic to the ordered list of tag names carried in that topic's payload. UPDATED 2026-08-07 (third revision) to add batch 2: topics g41-g73, the 33 tags that were previously available only from the StrideLinx router. They are being migrated to the CM5 so the StrideLinx Modbus data source can be removed from the machine network entirely -- see claude/stridelinx-modbus-polling.md for why. Note RejectPartsCount is NOT in batch 2: it is already configured at g20 and simply is not publishing, so the fix there is that row's Enable flag in C-more, not a second topic. Layout: 73 topics, g1..g73, in Publisher objects of exactly 10 topics each -- P1=g1..g10, P2=g11..g20, P3=g21..g30, P4=g31..g40, P5=g41..g50 (those five fill broker connection 1, which caps at 50 topics), then P6=g51..g60, P7=g61..g70, P8=g71..g73 on a SECOND broker connection. Batch 2 is ordered by production value, so importing only some Publisher objects still lands the most useful tags first. Every row is PayloadType=1 (raw tag value), so each list below has exactly one entry; the parser in mqtt_excel_logger_action.py splits on '|' and zips positionally, so it handles one value or several without code changes. This file and the TAG_BY_GROUP table inside cm5.html must be kept in sync.",
